  {
    "id": "ct_mcq_174",
    "type": "mcq",
    "topic_id": "integrated_challenge",
    "prerequisite_topics": [
      "math_alg_variations"
    ],
    "marks": 1,
    "difficulty": 6,
    "paper": 2,
    "section": "A",
    "question_en": "It is given that $z$ is the sum of two parts, one part varies directly as $x$ and the other part varies directly as $y^2$. When $x = 1, y = 2, z = 14$; when $x = 2, y = 1, z = 7$. Find $z$ when $x = 3, y = 3$.",
    "question_zh": "已知 $z$ 為兩部分之和，一部分隨 $x$ 正變，另一部分隨 $y^2$ 正變。當 $x = 1, y = 2, z = 14$；當 $x = 2, y = 1, z = 7$。求當 $x = 3, y = 3$ 時 $z$ 的值。",
    "options": [
      "A. 27",
      "B. 33",
      "C. 39",
      "D. 45"
    ],
    "correct_answer": "B",
    "solution_steps_en": [
      "Let $z = k_1 x + k_2 y^2$.",
      "Substituting (1, 2, 14): $k_1 + 4k_2 = 14$.",
      "Substituting (2, 1, 7): $2k_1 + k_2 = 7$.",
      "Solving the system: $k_2 = 7 - 2k_1$. Substitute: $k_1 + 4(7 - 2k_1) = 14 \\Rightarrow k_1 + 28 - 8k_1 = 14 \\Rightarrow -7k_1 = -14 \\Rightarrow k_1 = 2, k_2 = 3$.",
      "So $z = 2x + 3y^2$. When $x=3, y=3$, $z = 2(3) + 3(9) = 6 + 27 = 33$."
    ],
    "solution_steps_zh": [
      "設 $z = k_1 x + k_2 y^2$。",
      "代入 (1, 2, 14)：$k_1 + 4k_2 = 14$。",
      "代入 (2, 1, 7)：$2k_1 + k_2 = 7$。",
      "解方程組：$k_2 = 7 - 2k_1$。代入得 $k_1 + 4(7-2k_1) = 14 \\Rightarrow -7k_1 = -14 \\Rightarrow k_1 = 2, k_2 = 3$。",
      "因此 $z = 2x + 3y^2$。當 $x=3, y=3$ 時，$z = 6 + 27 = 33$。"
    ],
    "status": "approved"
  },
  {
    "id": "ct_mcq_175",
    "type": "mcq",
    "topic_id": "integrated_challenge",
    "prerequisite_topics": [
      "math_geo_coord"
    ],
    "marks": 1,
    "difficulty": 4,
    "paper": 2,
    "section": "A",
    "question_en": "If the point $P(2, -3)$ is rotated clockwise about the origin by $90^\\circ$ through the coordinates, and then translated left by 4 units, find the new coordinates of $P$.",
    "question_zh": "若將點 $P(2, -3)$ 繞原點按順時針方向旋轉 $90^\\circ$，然後向左平移 4 單位，求 $P$ 的新坐標。",
    "options": [
      "A. $(-7, -2)$",
      "B. $(-1, -2)$",
      "C. $(-7, 2)$",
      "D. $(-1, 2)$"
    ],
    "correct_answer": "A",
    "solution_steps_en": [
      "Clockwise rotation by $90^\\circ$ mapping: $(x, y) \\rightarrow (y, -x)$.",
      "For $P(2, -3)$, new is $(-3, -2)$.",
      "Translation left by 4 units: $x \\rightarrow x - 4$.",
      "New $x = -3 - 4 = -7$.",
      "New coordinates: $(-7, -2)$."
    ],
    "solution_steps_zh": [
      "順時針旋轉 $90^\\circ$ 的變換：$(x, y) \\rightarrow (y, -x)$。",
      "對於 $P(2, -3)$，旋轉後為 $(-3, -2)$。",
      "向左平移 4 單位：$x \\rightarrow x - 4$。",
      "新 $x = -3 - 4 = -7$。",
      "新坐標：$(-7, -2)$。"
    ],
    "status": "approved"
  },
  {
    "id": "ct_mcq_176",
    "type": "mcq",
    "topic_id": "integrated_challenge",
    "prerequisite_topics": [
      "math_alg_apgp",
      "math_alg_log_exp"
    ],
    "marks": 1,
    "difficulty": 7,
    "paper": 2,
    "section": "B",
    "question_en": "It is given that $x, y, z$ is a geometric progression with common ratio $r > 1$. If $\\log_y x, \\log_y y, \\log_y z$ is an arithmetic progression, find the common difference.",
    "question_zh": "已知 $x, y, z$ 為一個公比為 $r > 1$ 的等比數列。若 $\\log_y x, \\log_y y, \\log_y z$ 為一個等差數列，求該數列的公差。",
    "options": [
      "A. $\\log_y r$",
      "B. $\\log_r y$",
      "C. $1$",
      "D. $r$"
    ],
    "correct_answer": "A",
    "solution_steps_en": [
      "Let $x = y/r$ and $z = yr$。",
      "Then $\\log_y x = \\log_y (y/r) = \\log_y y - \\log_y r = 1 - \\log_y r$.",
      "And $\\log_y y = 1$; $\\log_y z = \\log_y (yr) = \\log_y y + \\log_y r = 1 + \\log_y r$.",
      "The terms are $1 - \\log_y r, 1, 1 + \\log_y r$.",
      "This is an AP with common difference $d = \\log_y r$."
    ],
    "solution_steps_zh": [
      "設 $x = y/r$ 及 $z = yr$。",
      "則 $\\log_y x = \\log_y (y/r) = 1 - \\log_y r$。",
      "$\\log_y y = 1$。",
      "$\\log_y z = 1 + \\log_y r$。",
      "該數列為 $1 - \\log_y r, 1, 1 + \\log_y r$。",
      "公差為 $\\log_y r$。"
    ],
    "status": "approved"
  },
  {
